/-!
# The inner-action family Δ₀

The source asserts that a member of Δ outside Δ₀ has relative Sylow two-order
two, that Δ₀ is nonempty, and that any conjugate of K containing an involution
inducing a nontrivial inner automorphism on L belongs to Δ₀.

The current development proves independence of the relative Sylow choice,
constructs the source intersection setup, and transports the families and the
order assertion under conjugation. The published detector proves (1) ⇒ (3).
The elementary and empty-case modules supply the faithful-centralizer argument
in case (I), the odd-intersection statement (*), and the product exclusion in
(+) leading to (!). The order assertion is still an explicit premise in the
last two reductions. The actual exceptional models are specified by group
isomorphisms and, for PSL₃(4), an intertwined graph-field action.

The remaining order-two cases, the outer-action reduction and the exceptional
model contradictions are needed before the three source conclusions can be
assembled here. No theorem in this module asserts that assembly is complete.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, 16.4.9,
printed pp.1188–1192.
-/
